--- !u!114 &1582563664344393250
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>Transparent glass.</b> The window glass is also <b>Transparent</b> (<i>Surface Type</i>), with an alpha of 0.75 in its Base Color, and it casts no shadows (<i>Mesh Renderer \u203A Lighting \u203A Cast Shadows: Off</i>), so the light from inside passes through."
--- !u!114 &2562438326077048090
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '<b>The plain materials</b>, with no maps: <i>GS-Steel</i> (metallic 1, smoothness 0.55: spouts, nozzles, keypads), <i>GS-Rubber</i> (almost black, smoothness 0.35: hoses and grips), <i>GS-Plastic-Sign</i> (pump sign panels), <i>GS-Asphalt-Far</i> (very dark, smoothness 0.6), and the two silhouette materials for the poles and wires.'
--- !u!114 &3571828394725082731
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Every surface uses <b>Universal Render Pipeline/Lit</b>, except the wet ground (\xA7 6) and the rain (\xA7 12). The textures are two sets from Poly Haven (CC0): <i>concrete_floor_worn_001</i> and <i>green_metal_rust</i>. Each set has an albedo map, a normal map, and a map that holds metallic and smoothness (the <i>\u2026-MetalSmooth.png</i> files in <i>Textures/URP/</i>, one per material, with the ambient occlusion in green)."
